/airi/commit/30b39b9b3f1cb2b169b478c1c7b0b391ac747f3b","commit_subject":"feat(stage-tamagotchi): replace native title bars with drawn title bars (#3298)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"andremichelle/openDAW","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-02T07:59:16Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"389224d34643857cf4d8763b5c43b1b0f5caa8e7","github_link":"https://github.com/andremichelle/openDAW/commit/389224d34643857cf4d8763b5c43b1b0f5caa8e7","commit_subject":"Hardware MIDI output keeps its timing while the page is busy (#356). Each note was timed from the moment the page picked it up, so UI work, garbage collection or a heavy frame pushed notes late by up to the length of the hold-up, and a note could even get shorter or lose its release. Notes now carry the exact audio time they belong to and are scheduled against the audio output clock, so a busy page no longer moves them, and timing is kept below a millisecond instead of being rounded to whole milliseconds. MIDI CC messages now get the device delay added like notes do, before they were sent too early or too late depending on where they fell in the audio block.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"moonbitlang/moon","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-02T07:59:13Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"b9dade6bc7f9376f6a4213b713db7707421c5268","github_link":"https://github.com/moonbitlang/moon/commit/b9dade6bc7f9376f6a4213b713db7707421c5268","commit_subject":"Merge pull request #2417 from moonbitlang/codex/moon-shared-cli-parser","ai_tool":"Codex"},{"repo_name":"moq-dev/moq","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-02T07:58:47Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"4fb80d85d72168a462b9ff8cfb54f6a3876dcc8f","github_link":"https://github.com/moq-dev/moq/commit/4fb80d85d72168a462b9ff8cfb54f6a3876dcc8f","commit_subject":"feat(net): expose a one-shot session's GOAWAY as `draining` (#7457)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-02T07:58:40Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"11907650552cc70d3d652de105078